    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey i need some help troubleshooting a sublimation issue. we've been running heat transfers for polyester blends but the color vibrancy is way lower than it should be and the edges look blurry. we are currently at 200c for 40 seconds with 4 bar of pressure. any idea what might be causing the poor transfer or the bleeding around the edges?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "There could be several reasons for the poor color vibrancy and edge bleeding in your sublimation transfers. Check if your ceramic sublimation blanks are free of dust or debris, as this can cause degradative particles to affect transfer quality. Also, the exposure time (40 seconds at 200°C) might be too long, or the pressure (4 bar) could be too strong, potentially causing over-processing. Additionally, the polyester blend might be prone to specific grade-specific limitations.",
